# Secora AI CLI — environment configuration
#
# The CLI's primary configuration is a persisted file (~/.pentesthub/config.json,
# written by `pentesthub login` — see src/config.ts's loadConfig()/saveConfig()).
# These two environment variables are an override layer on top of that file —
# useful for CI pipelines, containers, or one-off shell sessions where writing
# a config file to the user's home directory isn't desirable. Neither is
# required: with both unset, the CLI falls back to the config file, and any
# command that needs credentials it doesn't have prompts to run
# `pentesthub login` first.

# API key used instead of (takes precedence over) the entire config file —
# when set, the CLI authenticates with this key/baseUrl pair and never reads
# ~/.pentesthub/config.json at all. This is the recommended non-interactive/
# CI credential path (see packages/cli/README.md).
# PENTESTHUB_API_KEY=

# Base URL of the apps/api backend this CLI talks to. Overrides the config
# file's stored baseUrl when set; falls back to http://localhost:4000 if
# neither this nor a config file is present.
# PENTESTHUB_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000
